examples.question_text:
For $A(-2,3)$ and $B(4,-1)$, find $\overrightarrow{AB}$ as a column vector.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=7mm,y=7mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{gridink}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[xstep=7mm,ystep=7mm,gridink,thin] (-3,-2) grid (5,4);
\draw[->,black] (-3,0)--(5.3,0);
\draw[->,black] (0,-2)--(0,4.3);
\path (5.3,0) node[right] {$x$} (0,4.3) node[above] {$y$} (0,0) node[below left] {$O$};
\fill[black] (-2,3) circle (1.5pt) (4,-1) circle (1.5pt);
\path (-2,3) node[above left] {$A(-2,3)$} (4,-1) node[below] {$B(4,-1)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Subtract the initial position vector from the final position vector.

$\begin{aligned}\overrightarrow{AB}&=\overrightarrow{OB}-\overrightarrow{OA}\\&=\begin{pmatrix}4\\-1\end{pmatrix}-\begin{pmatrix}-2\\3\end{pmatrix}\\&=\begin{pmatrix}4-(-2)\\-1-3\end{pmatrix}\\&=\begin{pmatrix}6\\-4\end{pmatrix}\end{aligned}$

The sketch confirms a displacement of 6 units right and 4 units down.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=7mm,y=7mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{gridink}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\definecolor{answerblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{answerred}{HTML}{EF6068}
\draw[xstep=7mm,ystep=7mm,gridink,thin] (-3,-2) grid (5,4);
\draw[->,black] (-3,0)--(5.3,0);
\draw[->,black] (0,-2)--(0,4.3);
\path (5.3,0) node[right] {$x$} (0,4.3) node[above] {$y$} (0,0) node[below left] {$O$};
\draw[->,thick,answerblue] (-2,3)--(4,-1);
\draw[->,answerblue,dashed] (-2,3)--(4,3);
\draw[->,answerred,dashed] (4,3)--(4,-1);
\path (1,3) node[above] {$6$} (4,1) node[right] {$-4$};
\fill[black] (-2,3) circle (1.5pt) (4,-1) circle (1.5pt);
\path (-2,3) node[above left] {$A$} (4,-1) node[below] {$B$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

